# THE GREATNESS ENGINE
## Reconstructing Human Excellence
### Central Thesis
Greatness is not a single personality type.
It emerges through different combinations of:
perception, judgment, competence, action,
communication, responsibility, and transmission.
These are capabilities, not universal guarantees.
## THE MASTER LOOP
ENCOUNTER REALITY
    ↓
NOTICE A NEED, POSSIBILITY, OR CONTRADICTION
    ↓
DISTINGUISH EVIDENCE FROM INTERPRETATION
    ↓
IDENTIFY THE ACTUAL OBJECTIVE
    ↓
EXAMINE CONSTRAINTS AND ASSUMPTIONS
    ↓
SELECT AN INTERVENTION:
    - Improve the agent
    - Improve the tool
    - Improve the environment
    - Improve the method
    - Improve the rules
    - Improve coordination
    ↓
PROTOTYPE / PRACTICE / ACT
    ↓
MEASURE THE CONSEQUENCES
    ↓
REVISE OR RETREAT WHEN WARRANTED
    ↓
DEMONSTRATE AND COMMUNICATE
    ↓
TEACH / REPLICATE / INSTITUTIONALIZE
    ↓
AUDIT COSTS, HARMS, AND EXTERNALITIES
    ↓
UPDATE THE OBJECTIVE OR MODEL
    ↺
## THE TEN CORE INVARIANTS
G01 — OBSERVE BEFORE EXPLAINING
Distinguish signals from assumptions.
G02 — PRESERVE PURPOSE, REVISE METHODS
Loyalty to a goal need not require loyalty
to an obsolete implementation.
G03 — SEARCH THE INTERFACE
Changing a tool, environment, or
representation may change capability.
G04 — EMBODY THE KNOWLEDGE
Competence may be expressed through
movement, performance, craft, and action.
G05 — MAKE REALITY THE JUDGE
Use tests that can correct expectations.
G06 — COMMUNICATE THROUGH DEMONSTRATION
Allow observable behavior to support
articulated vision.
G07 — BUILD COMPLEMENTARY TEAMS
Exceptional achievements are often
produced by networks of specialists.
G08 — MAKE MASTERY TRANSMISSIBLE
Convert personal excellence into
teachable, reusable methods.
G09 — PRESERVE THE ABILITY TO SELF-CORRECT
No success makes a method or model sacred.
G10 — ACCOUNT FOR CONSEQUENCES
Evaluate who benefits, who bears the
costs, and what remains after the actor.
## META-INVARIANT
A person may create lasting value by:
DISCOVERING what is hidden;
INVENTING what is missing;
IMPROVING what is flawed;
PROTECTING what is vulnerable;
COMMUNICATING what is misunderstood;
or TEACHING what others can carry forward.
None of these requires superiority
in every dimension of human life.
## FAILURE GUARDS
NOVELTY != IMPROVEMENT
CONFIDENCE != COMPETENCE
CHARISMA != CHARACTER
PERSISTENCE != JUDGMENT
SUCCESS != MORAL JUSTIFICATION
VISIBILITY != VALUE
CORRELATION != CAUSATION
STORY != VERIFIED HISTORY
DEMONSTRATION != UNIVERSAL PROOF
INSPIRATION != IMPLEMENTATION
